.Dd September 8, 2026
.Dt BOSD 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm bosd
.Nd on-screen display engine
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl h
.Op Fl n Ar instance
.Bro Fl d | Fl C Brc
.Nm
.Op Fl Dho
.Op Fl n Ar instance
.Op Fl a Ar text
.Op Fl b Ar badge
.Op Fl p Ar text
.Op Fl s Ar scale
.Op Fl x Ar offset
.Op Fl y Ar offset
.Bro Ar icon | Fl c Ar countdown | Fl t Ar text Brc
.Op Ar hold_seconds
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
paints a PNG glyph, scaled to the panel and outlined for
legibility, in a centered click-through ARGB32 overlay window.
The overlay is centered on the primary output, falling back to the
first connected internal panel (eDP/LVDS/DSI), then the whole X
screen.
Countdown digits
.Pq Fl c
and short outlined text
.Pq Fl t
draw in the same overlay.
.Nm
is the display engine behind media-key and hotkey feedback: a
warm daemon owns the window, and clients replace the visible show
in place, so rapid key repeats never flash.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width "-n instance"
.It Fl a Ar text
Caption below the artwork: a smaller outlined line under the
glyph, digits, or text, e.g.
.Dq airplane mode off
under the airplane glyph.
Escapes decode as with
.Fl t ;
literal whitespace is permitted.
At most 63 characters before decoding.
.It Fl b Ar badge
Draw
.Ar badge
as a superscript at the glyph's upper right \(em white with a black
outline, about a quarter of the glyph height.
Used for index digits and short labels
.Pq e.g. a headphone number, Dq All .
At most 31 characters before decoding; literal whitespace is not
permitted.
Escapes decode as with
.Fl t ,
so
.Ql a\ex20b
badges as
.Dq a b .
.It Fl C
Clear the channel's active render \(em hide an in-progress show,
such as a long countdown or an indefinite (\-1) hold \(em and
return immediately.
Without a running daemon there is nothing to clear.
.It Fl c Ar countdown
Count down from
.Ar countdown
to 1 in huge outlined digits on a full-panel overlay, one second
per digit
.Pq Ar hold_seconds overrides ,
then exit \(em the screenshot timer.
Replaces
.Ar icon
and is dispatched to the channel daemon like any show, replacing
whatever it displays (and vice versa); without a daemon the
invoking process draws it and returns when done.
Honors
.Fl b , o , s , x ,
and
.Fl y :
the badge rides the digits' upper right and
.Fl s
scales the digits.
.It Fl D
Render directly in the invoking process, ignoring any running
channel daemon, and exit when the hold elapses.
Useful for trying a show without disturbing what the daemon
displays, or for pacing an animation from a script.
.It Fl d
Run as the display daemon for
.Ar instance ,
listening on a per-user datagram socket.
.It Fl h
Print usage and exit.
.It Fl n Ar instance
Select the OSD channel (default
.Dq Li default ) .
Independent channels own independent windows and sockets.
.It Fl o
Skip the black outline normally drawn behind the glyph for
legibility on any wallpaper.
Suited to full-color artwork that carries its own contrast.
.It Fl p Ar text
Caption above the artwork, otherwise as
.Fl a ,
e.g.
.Dq Shutdown in
over a countdown, with
.Fl b Li s
marking seconds.
.It Fl s Ar scale
Multiply the panel-derived render size by
.Ar scale
(0.1 to 8.0, default 1.0).
The glyph is normally sized from the panel height, independent of
the PNG's native resolution;
.Fl s Li 2.0
renders it twice that size.
.It Fl t Ar text
Draw
.Ar text
in the countdown's giant outlined style, centered on the panel and
held like an icon show \(em e.g. the checkmark confirming a
screenshot.
Replaces
.Ar icon
and is dispatched like any show.
Escapes decode before rendering:
.Ql \ex Ns Ar NN
a raw byte,
.Ql \eu Ns Ar NNNN
and
.Ql \eU Ns Ar NNNNNNNN
a Unicode codepoint (UTF-8 encoded), and
.Ql \e\e
a backslash \(em so
.Fl t Ql \eu2713
draws the checkmark.
Literal whitespace is not permitted; embed it as
.Ql \ex20 .
Honors
.Fl b , o , s , x ,
and
.Fl y .
.It Fl x Ar offset
Shift the artwork horizontally by
.Ar offset
pixels from panel center: positive right, negative left.
Placement semantics are those of
.Fl y .
.It Fl y Ar offset
Shift the artwork vertically by
.Ar offset
pixels from panel center: positive down, negative up
.Pq X11 coordinate sense .
Consumers sharing a screen with fixed chrome (e.g. a taskbar) can
recenter within the remaining space, such as
.Fl y Li -20
above a 40-pixel bottom bar.
Offset placement is exact; artwork carried past a panel edge is
clipped at the edge rather than shown on a neighboring output,
so a large offset slides a show in from beyond it.
Only offset-free shows are clamped to remain fully visible.
.El
.Pp
Without
.Fl d ,
.Nm
sends a show request to the running daemon for the channel; if no
daemon is alive, it paints the glyph itself and exits when
.Ar hold_seconds
(default 2.0, clamped to 0.01\(en30) elapse.
A
.Ar hold_seconds
of \-1 holds the show until it is replaced or cleared with
.Fl C ;
without a daemon, until interrupted (e.g. Ctrl-C).
It does not apply to
.Fl c ,
whose digits must advance.
.Sh ICON RESOLUTION
An
.Ar icon
containing a slash is used as a path.
A bare name is searched in each directory of the colon-separated
.Ev BOSD_PATH ,
then in the compiled share directory.
A
.Pa .png
suffix is appended when missing.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width "BOSD_PATH"
.It Ev BOSD_PATH
Colon-separated icon search path, tried before the compiled default.
.It Ev DISPLAY
X11 display to draw on.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/tmp/bosd.instance.uid.sock" -compact
.It Pa /tmp/bosd. Ns Ar instance . Ns Ar uid Ns Pa .sock
show-request socket
.It Pa /tmp/bosd. Ns Ar instance . Ns Ar uid Ns Pa .pid
daemon pid
.It Pa /usr/local/share/bosd
default icon directory
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Warm the airplane-mode channel at session start:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
bosd -n airplane -d &
.Ed
.Pp
Flash the on glyph for 1.5 seconds:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
bosd -n airplane airplane-on 1.5
.Ed
.Pp
Show the second headphone output:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
bosd -n audio -b 2 audio-headphones 1.5
.Ed
.Pp
Screenshot flow: count down from 3, capture, confirm with a
checkmark:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
bosd -n shot -c 3
scrot screenshot.png
bosd -n shot -t '\eu2713' 1
.Ed
.Pp
Clear whatever the channel is showing:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
bosd -n shot -C
.Ed
.Pp
Shutdown warning: caption over a 10-second countdown, badge
marking seconds:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
bosd -n power -p 'Shutdown in' -b s -c 10
.Ed
.Pp
Caption a glyph:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
bosd -n airplane -a 'airplane mode off' airplane-off
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr xrandr 1
